  "details": "Currently, if you send /input/GrabRight (or left), and the user's hand is in proximity to both a physbone and a pickup (whether that's a personal mirror, item, or world pickup), the pickup is always prioritized. \n\nThis causes issues for VRCBitetech, because the grab point is moved to the face, and the user is less focused on where their hand might be. Grabbing physbones is tied to the hand collider, which we are able to move, however pickups are tied to where the controller is, which we cannot move. This means that when a user attempts to bite a physbone, it can in some cases instead grab a pickup close to the user's hand, and biting the physbone fails. \n\nI think that there are two decent options for fixing this:\n\n1 - As the title says, separate the endpoints for grabbing physbones and grabbing pickups. This way, VRCBitetech can simply send the signal to grab physbones, and pickups will not interfere.\n\n2 - Allow the location of the pickup grabbing location to be moved dynamically. This way, VRCBitetech would also allow users to bite pickups, which would be a very very welcome feature.",
